                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "DISCLAMER: I only recommend buying it during sales to people who played the game (or similar games like prehistorik) in the 90s and collectors: graphics are barely decent, music and sounds are pretty disturbing and it really has not aged well. It is overpriced too, to be honest.\n\nBUT: this game was developed by a handful of people and it gave me lots of fun in the old days. It still is fun enough and rich in enemy mechanics and secrets. Games used to be extremely difficult and completing them (or even reaching a new level) was rewarding as hell, this game is no exception. As for sounds, be patient: almost nobody had a sound card when it was initially released and that chiptune-like music sounded awesome with a croaking case speaker.  :)",
